// vimcheck.nv — names every module of the package that a program may use,
// so that building the package as a library checks all of them.
//
// A library has no `main`, and the compiler leaves out a module that every
// `use` naming it has removed (SPEC section 9.6, the dead-module rule).
// `vimstep` holds a `use vimram` behind a false condition, and `vimstep` is
// named by `vimram` alone, so with nothing else naming it the whole package
// would be left out and `novo pkg build` would check none of it.  A module
// that no `use` names stays, so this one stays, and its `use` lines keep the
// modules below it.  It holds no code and a program that names none of them
// gets no code from it.  `vimram` is not named here on purpose: it is the
// module that a program must ask for, and the test suites do.

use vimtext
use vimmodal
use vimkey
use vimmotion
use vimobject
use vimscroll
use vimedit
use viminsert
use vimnormal
use vimstep
